JavaScript implements menus/modals/view switches/status and theme behavior. CSS class detection needs complete class names: use explicit maps rather than assembling bg-${color}-500. React uses props/state and className composition with the same discipline. The executable lab example is vanilla JavaScript; a React component is provided as source for an external configured React project, not falsely executed as JSX in QuickJS. Modal/menu keyboard behavior and focus remain part of accessible implementation, not styling alone.

